Léa, a toddler girl of stocky build with brown eyes, brown straight chin-length hair with loose bangs at her eyebrows, wearing a red wool knit cardigan over a white long-sleeve T-shirt, grey corduroy trousers, and brown leather ankle boots, tugs firmly on the long grey wool overcoat sleeve of Henri. Henri, an elderly man with a slim build, stooped posture, brown eyes, gray wavy short combed hair, and a full white beard, wearing a long grey wool overcoat, an orange knitted wool scarf, a blue checked cotton shirt, brown corduroy trousers, and black leather lace-up shoes, stands beside her looking down into her face with raised brows and a calm mouth. Léa looks up at Henri with her brows pulled tight, eyes wide with fear, and mouth open in worry. Flat on the dark timber boards of the covered bridge walkway at Léa's feet lies l'ombre, a solid near-black shadow silhouette with long thin limbs, no facial features, and a smooth rounded head, stretching along the wet wood. Overhead, the dark timber truss frame of the covered wooden bridge encloses the walkway, with fallen autumn leaves scattered across the wet boards against the timber walls, while dusk light filters through the slatted side openings. In the distant background, a small passer-by in a dark green coat walks away toward the far opening. Medium shot.

---METADATA---
