Léa, a stocky toddler girl with straight brown chin-length hair and bangs, dressed in a red wool knit cardigan, white long-sleeve T-shirt, grey corduroy trousers, and brown leather boots, stands on the grey pavement of the castle street beside the Landvogteischloss. She faces forward, looking directly out with bright brown eyes, lifted brows, and a happy open smile. Beside her on the pavement, l'ombre stands as a full-length flat near-black silhouette with long thin limbs, facing forward in step with her. Behind them rises the stone stepped-gable castle with its round stair turret, adjacent to the covered wooden bridge spanning the river beneath forested hills rich with autumn foliage under the soft dusk sky. Wide shot, with generous open space in the upper portion of the frame.

---METADATA---
